*> Acceptance test of the selector options the command resolver evaluates (docs/protocol/15-commands-framework.md §7; 16 §3.4): distance,
*> the volume (x y z dx dy dz, negative extents too), level, gamemode, name, team, tag, type, x_rotation, y_rotation, sort and limit over players
*> and over the mobs of the core (kill @e, kill @n); the options this resolver cannot evaluate (nbt, scores, advancements, predicate) are
*> cobolcraft.selector.unsupported [option]. The count is the result of msg (players) or kill (mobs). Opal holds operator status and stands at
*> 0 64 0, Alice at 10 64 0 in creative mode with yaw 90 and pitch -45, Bob at 20 64 0 with yaw 200.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-CMD-SELECTORS.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY COREAPI.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-ID-OPAL           BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID-ALICE          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID-BOB            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(16).
 01 WS-NAME-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LINE                PIC X(768).
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(4096).
 01 WS-DISCARD             PIC X(4096).
 01 WS-EXPECTED            PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-EXPECTED-N          BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-NUM                 BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-RESULT              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 4096.
